BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (Use eight transport operating plays to define initial service scope, with contingency recovery as the ninth) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (adjacent play. These labels organize this chapter's execution map rather than claiming additional supplied) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm (catalog identifiers. Standing-order NEMT illustrates the core economics: 20 completed trips at $60 produce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm ($1,200 billings, $660 driver settlements, and $540 retained contribution before overhead. Workers') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (compensation transport requires adjuster authorization and accepted mileage terms; discharge transport) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (requires a clear wait-time clock and a facility escalation contact. Recurring specimen routes can produce) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm ($1,000 billings from five $200 route-days, with $550 settlements and $450 retained under the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (illustrative split. STAT coverage needs a priced backup rather than an unfunded promise. Owner-operator) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (capacity management maintains verified availability; GPS evidence and clean-claim collection complete the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (remaining two plays. If a $200 route needs an extra $80 rescue payment, its $90 planned contribution falls) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (to $10. That loss must remain visible in route economics. The 45% share is the canonical aggregate) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (assumption, not a mandated payment arrangement for every job. Reject lanes whose actual settlement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm (terms, deadhead mileage, or required staffing cannot support the modeled contribution.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (Treat hospital_lien_medical_receivables_arbitrage, the TRACK_1 Out-of-Network Medical Claim & ERISA) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (Appeal Contingency Recovery play, as a separate contracted service rather than dispatch float. Surgical) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (centers, specialty clinics, and air ambulance operators may supply underpaid commercial claims, but federal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 441.95 Tm (No Surprises Act IDR eligibility depends on service, coverage, jurisdiction, and payment circumstances.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 426.72 Tm (Ground ambulance claims are generally outside federal NSA IDR; assess contractual, state, or applicable) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 411.50 Tm (benefit-appeal routes instead. Use trained specialists to screen eligibility and automate documents and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 396.27 Tm (deadlines, not to assume every denial qualifies. Federal open negotiation generally must be initiated within) Tj ET
